{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_DGyUfCm39zbmdTAWgT7DhSoD","content":"Title: GitHub - Sladck/trainingpeaks-to-intervals-icu: Sync planned TrainingPeaks workouts to intervals.icu with structured power/pace/HR targets\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-05-20\nURL: https://github.com/Sladck/trainingpeaks-to-intervals-icu\nSnippet: What it syncs Permalink: What it syncs |TrainingPeaks side|becomes on intervals.icu| |-|-| |Planned workout (Bike / Run / Swim / MTB / Strength / …)|`WORKOUT` event with sport-correct type| |Structured intervals ( `%FTP`, `%LTHR`, `%threshold pace`)|`workout_doc` with absolute watts / bpm / s/km, computed from your TP thresholds| |Workout `description` (coach text)|event description (+ pushed into paired `activity.description`)| |`coachComments`|\"Coach:\" section in description| |`workoutComments\n\n---\n\nTitle: GitHub - platypus45/domestique: Adaptive cycling training planner: 7 science-grounded injury-prevention guardrails close the loop between planned and actual training. 4,232 ZWO workouts, 622 routes, h\nSite: Github\nDate: 2026-10-23\nURL: https://github.com/platypus45/domestique\nSnippet: Train by heart rate (no power meter) - Switch the target mode in Settings (Power ↔ Heart rate). The heart-rate option unlocks once your LTHR (lactate-threshold heart rate) is known — Domestique keeps it synced automatically from your intervals.icu ride data, unless you've set it manually, in which case your number stays put. - Steady aerobic work gets real bpm ranges, derived from the standard Coggan %FTP ↔ %LTHR zone table — so an endurance ride reads as an actual heart-rate range, not a percen\n\n---\n\nTitle: intervals-mcp by ale7canna\nSite: glama.ai\nDate: 2026-08-20\nURL: https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/ale7canna/intervals-mcp\nSnippet: Troubleshooting: l'allenamento arriva sul Garmin senza target Sintomo: sull'orologio gli step ci sono, con distanze e nomi giusti, ma ognuno mostra \"No Target\". Su intervals.icu il `workout_doc` sembra perfetto. Causa: manca la soglia del tipo di target usato nelle sport settings di quello sport (threshold pace per il passo, FTP per la potenza). In quel caso intervals.icu elimina i target dal file che manda al dispositivo — anche quando l'allenamento usa valori assoluti, dove la soglia non servi\n\n---\n\nTitle: Convert training prescriptions to Intervals.icu workouts with Claude Opus AI | n8n workflow template\nSite: n8n.io\nDate: 2025-12-11\nURL: https://n8n.io/workflows/9822-convert-training-prescriptions-to-intervalsicu-workouts-with-claude-opus-ai/\nSnippet: See llms.txt for all machine-readable content. Last update Last update 6 months ago Categories Share --- Description Transform training prescriptions into perfectly formatted Intervals.icu workouts using AI. This workflow automatically converts free-text workout descriptions into structured interval training sessions with proper heart rate zones, pace calculations, and exercise formatting. What this workflow does 1. Collects workout details via a web form (date, title, and workout description) 2\n\n---\n\nTitle: garmin-mcp-bridge | MCP Servers\nSite: lobehub.com\nDate: 2026-07-19\nURL: https://lobehub.com/it/mcp/jonas-theobald-garmin-mcp-bridge\nSnippet: Writing workouts Permalink for this section The workout_doc trap Permalink for this section Never include a `workout_doc` field in the payload. A planned workout only syncs to your watch if Intervals.icu parsed the description into structured steps. What triggers that parsing is undocumented, and the intuitive guess is wrong: sending `workout_doc: {}` to _request_ parsing actually suppresses it. The server reads the presence of the field as \"steps already supplied\" and skips the parser. The work\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals Workout · GarminFans\nSite: GarminFans\nDate: 2026-11-07\nURL: https://www.garminfans.com/fi/apps/8f9714b5-9367-4424-b086-30711f0d9632/\nSnippet: Kuvaus Intervals Workout is a Data Field for Edge 540 and 1050 that reads your Intervals.icu structured workout and guides you in real time, step by step. At a glance: • Current target watts (blue) + 3s actual power (green/red at ±15 W) • Heart rate color-coded by zone (gray, blue, green, orange, red by % of threshold) • Cadence with target (e.g. \"target 90 rpm\") — green ±5, orange ±10, red beyond • Step name + position (e.g. \"Ramp 50 to 75 %FTP 1/10\") • Step time remaining + total time • Per-st\n\n---\n\nTitle: Complete guide to Intervals.icu for cyclists\nSite: jscyclingtraining.com\nDate: 2026-10-05\nURL: https://jscyclingtraining.com/en/complete-guide-intervals-icu-cyclists/\nSnippet: Create and plan workouts To plan a session, click on a day, choose the sport and describe the workout. The interesting part is that the builder understands plain text: you can write the session directly and the platform interprets it. The pattern is simple: duration or distance followed by the target, for example “10m 65%” or “4x 5m 105%, 5m 50%”. Targets can be expressed as a percentage of FTP, a zone, absolute watts, heart rate —marked with HR or LTHR— or pace. You can also add cadence and ste\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu Workout Format — ZonePace\nURL: https://zonepace.cc/intervals-workout-format\nSnippet: Overview The Intervals.icu workout format is a plain-text syntax that describes steps with duration or distance and intensity targets. It supports cycling (power), running (pace) and heart rate targets, and you can mix modes within a single workout. Time & Distance Time - `h` hours: `1h` - `m` minutes: `10m`, `5m` - `s` seconds: `30s`, `90s` - Combined: `1m30` - Shorthand: `5'` (5 min), `30\"` (30 sec), `1'30\"` Distance - `km`: `2km`, `10km` - `mi`: `1mi`, `4.5mi` Note: `m` means minutes, not met\n\n---\n\nTitle: Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\nSite: Worklore\nDate: 2026-05-12\nURL: https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts\nSnippet: Reproduce this Prerequisites: an Intervals.icu account with API access (OAuth token or API key), athlete thresholds configured in Intervals (LTHR at minimum), and a Garmin watch that syncs workouts from Intervals via Garmin Connect. Your agent will need from you: your Intervals athlete id and API credential; your LTHR as stored in Intervals; permission to create (and later delete) a test calendar event. Steps: 1. Create an event via `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` with `workout_doc.steps`, wh\n\n---\n\nTitle: Domestique - a free, open source, science based, self hosted cycling training app - Training - TrainerRoad\nSite: TrainerRoad\nDate: 2026-06-14\nURL: https://www.trainerroad.com/forum/t/domestique-a-free-open-source-science-based-self-hosted-cycling-training-app/113958\nSnippet: post by Domestique1 on Jul 6 100% Free, open source, locally hosted training cycling planner. Science based. What’s new since the last post, grouped: Train by heart rate — no power meter needed. The biggest addition. A workout-targets mode that prescribes every session in bpm: LTHR-anchored ranges for steady work, RPE for short maximal efforts (HR lags too much there, and the app tells you so instead of pretending). LTHR syncs continuously from intervals.icu with a manual override, zones are cus\n\n---\n\nTitle: intervals.icu setup guide — Coach AMA\nURL: https://coach-ama.com/guide/intervals\nSnippet: Get your training data flowing to Coach AMA In the same Connections box, enable Upload planned workouts when your service supports it. This is the return path that sends Coach AMA's [AMA] sessions from the intervals.icu calendar to your training app or head unit. 1. ## 4. If you ride in Zwift Connect the Zwift box and enable both Download activities and Upload planned workouts. In Zwift, find synced sessions under Workouts → Custom → Intervals.icu; today's session may also appear on the home scr\n\n---\n\nTitle: Sync with Intervals.icu - General - Athletica Forum\nSite: athletica.ai\nDate: 2025-08-03\nURL: https://forum.athletica.ai/t/sync-with-intervals-icu/2454/135\nSnippet: Firestop's profile Got it @holkatriatlonka…now I understand! Part of the issue appears to be resident in _intervals.icu_…looking at its “ Workout Builder”, it does not have an option to accept specific Pace values as an input for adding intervals to workouts ( see attached) unlike the option for inputting intervals based on Power (2nd photo). This input limitation in _interval.icu_ may provide _Athletica_ a challenge, but they have solved it with inputting interval HR values in _intervals.icu_ a\n\n---\n\nTitle: Power and HR targets for Garmin workouts - Announcements - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2021-02-14\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/power-and-hr-targets-for-garmin-workouts/2926\nSnippet: post by david on Feb 14, 2021 You can now specify power and HR targets for workout steps (default is lap power and lap HR): This sorts out the issue with HR steps not working on Garmin watches (well at least some of them). You need to choose “Instant HR” (hr=1s in the text): - warmup 30s 50% LTHR hr=1s - Wibble 20m 78% LTHR hr=1s - cooldown 30s 40% LTHR hr=1s 4 months later\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_4fKoRvwdrycZ8mmK2f5SinrT","content":"Title: GitHub - LetsLearntocodeforfun/Apollo-Running: Free, local-first marathon training app for desktop and web. 33 training plans (Higdon, Pfitzinger, Daniels, Hansons, FIRST, Galloway and more), direct G\nSite: Github\nURL: https://github.com/LetsLearntocodeforfun/Apollo-Running\nSnippet: Why Apollo - Free sync with every major platform — Connect Garmin Connect directly with your own free personal API key (desktop app): every activity, with routes, splits and laps from your watch's original files, and no other account in between. Or connect a free intervals.icu account and Apollo pulls every run, ride, and swim recorded on COROS, Suunto, Polar, Wahoo, Zwift, and more — full history on the first sync, incremental after that. Prefer zero accounts? Drag in FIT/GPX/TCX files or your \n\n---\n\nTitle: FIT workout import silently drops REPS steps and mis-scales DISTANCE steps - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-08-21\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/fit-workout-import-silently-drops-reps-steps-and-mis-scales-distance-steps/131081\nSnippet: t at all. hr_zone target exports as a wrong absolute range: a workout_doc step with hr: {value: 2, units: \"hr_zone\"} (real HR zone 2) exported ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts — start/end, not value/end\nSite: Worklore\nDate: 2026-05-12\nURL: https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts\nSnippet: Reproduce this Prerequisites: an Intervals.icu account with API access (OAuth token or API key), athlete thresholds configured in Intervals (LTHR at minimum), and a Garmin watch that syncs workouts from Intervals via Garmin Connect. Your agent will need from you: your Intervals athlete id and API credential; your LTHR as stored in Intervals; permission to create (and later delete) a test calendar event. Steps: 1. Create an event via `POST /api/v1/athlete/{id}/events` with `workout_doc.steps`, wh\n\n---\n\nTitle: Training Plans in Intervals.icu — Create, Share & Export\nSite: STAS\nDate: 2026-04-05\nURL: https://stas.run/en/guides/intervals-icu-training-plans\nSnippet: When you apply it, choose your target race date — Intervals.icu back-fills ... Wahoo ELEMNT head units connect via Settings → Connections → Wahoo.\n\n---\n\nTitle: \nSite: Polar Global\nURL: https://support.polar.com/e_manuals/Team_Pro/Polar_Team_Pro_user_manual_Deutsch/manual.pdf\nSnippet: Sieh die RR-Intervalle, d. h. die Zeit zwischen aufeinanderfolgenden Herzschlägen, von Herzfrequenzdaten aus Trainingseinheiten oder Spielen auf einer Grafik an. Du kannst in der Grafik vergrößern und Datenbereiche zur weiteren Analyse eingrenzen. Die angezeigten Informationen umfassen min. RRIntervall, max. RR-Intervall, Ø RR-Intervall und Herzfrequenz-Variabilität (RMSSD). DATEN EXPORTIEREN Exportiere Daten für Trainingseinheiten im XLS- oder CSV-Format. Du kannst die Daten des gesamten Teams \n\n---\n\nTitle: Import Your Own Training Plan Into Garmin With Intervals.icu\nSite: VAW.BE\nDate: 2026-10-27\nURL: https://garmin.vaw.be/en/community/day-84-import-training-plan-to-garmin\nSnippet: Day 84: Import Your Own Training Plan Into Garmin With Intervals.icu Step 3: turn your schedule into upload-ready JSON ``` You are a training plan converter. Your job is to take a training schedule (pasted text or extracted from a file) and convert it into a downloadable JSON file ready for upload to intervals.icu via API. --- STEP 1 — PARSE THE PLAN Read the training schedule carefully. Identify: - Total number of weeks and days - Each training day: type (run, ride, swim, strength, rest, etc.),\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
